        <div class="steps-grid">
          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-num">01 · STANDBY CHECK</div>
            <h3>SQLite liveness</h3>
            <p>Checks <code>program_start_time.db</code> and <code>heartbeat_cache.db</code>. Exits immediately if an active host is healthy with time remaining.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-num">02 · WARMUP</div>
            <h3>Pre-lock bootstrap</h3>
            <p>Starts <code>MarketDataStreamManager</code>, OHLCV datasets, consumer loops, and venue clients at low priority before taking the lock.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-num">03 · RECOVERY</div>
            <h3>Lock &amp; disk restore</h3>
            <p>Acquires <code>/tmp/live_infra_state_lock</code>, runs <code>recover_state_from_disk()</code> for open orders/trades, and marks the engine ready.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-num">04 · CONTROL LOOP</div>
            <h3>Hot-sync &amp; watchdogs</h3>
            <p>Bumps dead-man's-switch heartbeat, hot-diffs PostgreSQL strategy rows, checks <code>QuoteHolds</code>, and reconciles orders and inventory.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-num">05 · HANDOFF</div>
            <h3>Graceful shutdown</h3>
            <p>On <code>SIGTERM</code> or max runtime, pulls resting entry quotes, flushes state to disk and Postgres, and releases the lock to the standby.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

