      <!-- 4. Core Internals -->
      <section class="band" id="internals">
        <div class="sec-head">
          <div class="kicker">04 · Internals</div>
          <h2>Memory layout, fill simulation, and numerics</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="internals-grid">
          <div class="spec-card">
            <h3><code>RingBufferBook</code></h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Flat tick-indexed array hashed by <code>tick_idx &amp; mask</code> instead of tree nodes.</li>
              <li>16-byte POD slots (<code>tick_tag</code>, <code>updated_sec</code>, <code>qty</code>); tag mismatch rejects stale wrapped slots.</li>
              <li>64-bit occupancy bitmap skips empty ranges with <code>__builtin_ctzll</code>.</li>
              <li>Allocated with <code>make_unique_for_overwrite</code> so untouched pages use zero physical RAM (19-bit exchange / 10-bit Polymarket window, 16 KB per side).</li>
              <li><code>apply_bid</code> benchmarks at ~1.5 ns/op on Intel Core Ultra 9 285K.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="spec-card">
            <h3><code>BacktestState</code> vs <code>PaperExchange</code></h3>
            <ul>
              <li><code>BacktestState</code> replays Parquet events in timestamp order with latency, maker/taker fees, leverage, and Polymarket queue-notional tracking.</li>
              <li><code>PaperExchange</code> runs on a dedicated thread inside <code>live_infra</code> against live feeds.</li>
              <li>Paper taker orders evaluate at <code>ack + latency</code> with <code>PAPER_SLIPPAGE_BPS</code> (default <code>3</code>).</li>
              <li>Resting remainders fill as maker against quotes and subsequent prints; cancels stop later fills immediately.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="spec-card">
            <h3>Numerics &amp; process model</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>All C++ targets compile with <code>-fno-fast-math -fno-strict-aliasing -ffp-contract=off -frounding-math</code>.</li>
              <li>Quantities, fees, and realized PnL use <code>mpfr::mpreal</code> over dynamically linked MPFR/GMP.</li>
              <li><code>Core::Engine</code> is a process-wide singleton matching the one-process-per-host model.</li>
              <li><code>trading_engine</code> headers reside under <code>include/market_making/</code>.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

